---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Shemar Marks handles project inquiries, reference submissions, permissions, and privacy-respectful website measurement."
>
  <PageHero
    label="PRIVACY / UPDATED 2 NOVEMBER 2026"
    title="Your details."
    accent="Handled with care."
    description="This notice explains how information submitted through this website is used. For questions or requests, contact hello@shemarmarks.com."
  />
  <section class="section wrap prose">
    <h2>Who handles your information.</h2>
    <p>
      Shemar Marks is an independent consultant based in Jamaica. Contact{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@shemarmarks.com">hello@shemarmarks.com</a> about access, correction,
      deletion, or withdrawing a reference.
    </p>
    <h2>Inquiries.</h2>
    <p>
      The inquiry form collects your name, email, project details, selected service, timeline, and
      any optional company, website, or budget information you provide. It also records the
      submitting page, CTA, and submission time. When measurement is enabled, it also records the
      first landing page, referrer, coarse traffic source, and campaign parameters. This information
      is used to respond, scope work, and understand which pages generate useful inquiries.
    </p>
    <p>
      Submissions are stored at the edge before an attempt to synchronize them to a private CRM or
      send an acknowledgment. Cloudflare provides hosting, spam protection, and storage. Google
      Workspace delivers acknowledgment emails through the configured Gmail integration; Resend is
      an optional alternative when configured. These providers may process information outside your
      country.
    </p>
    <h2>References.</h2>
    <p>
      Reference submissions are private until reviewed and approved. Your email is never part of the
      public reference. Your name, title, and company are displayed only with identity permission. A
      project value requires permission or an authorized owner entry, plus separate publication
      approval. You can request correction or removal by email.
    </p>
    <h2>Security and retention.</h2>
    <p>
      Please do not submit passwords, tokens, or sensitive business records. Access to submissions
      is restricted. Spam-prevention counters use a short-lived salted hash of the network address
      rather than retaining the raw address in the application database. Website-held inquiries
      older than 365 days are automatically removed after delivery to the private CRM is confirmed;
      undelivered inquiries remain available for recovery. Pending, rejected, and needs-changes
      references older than 365 days are also removed. Approved references remain until removed.
      Copies in the CRM or email are handled separately and may need to be retained for operational
      or contractual reasons. Contact me to request removal.
    </p>
    <h2>Website measurement.</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Web Analytics can provide aggregate page measurement when enabled. First-party
      event counts record page views and interactions without persistent visitor identifiers. A
      coarse Google or Bing organic-search category is inferred from the referrer or explicit
      organic campaign tags and retained within the current tab; aggregate counts store only the
      event name, page path, day, and count. Search terms and full referrer URLs are not sent with
      interaction events. Form attribution distinguishes search, direct, referral, paid, and tagged
      campaign arrivals using session storage within the current tab. These categories are
      estimates, not verified identities. Do Not Track, Global Privacy Control, and the preference
      below disable first-party interaction measurement and retention of this optional first-visit
      context.
    </p>
    <div class="privacy-controls">
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input id="analytics-optout" type="checkbox" />
        Disable first-party interaction measurement on this device.
      </label>
      <p class="small">
        This stores a local preference. Essential spam protection and the details you submit in an
        inquiry still apply.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h2>External links.</h2>
    <p>
      Links to GitHub, LinkedIn, X, and other third parties are governed by those services’ own
      notices. Clicking an email link opens your chosen email application.
    </p>
  </section>
  <script>
    const checkbox = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#analytics-optout');
    if (checkbox) {
      try {
        checkbox.checked = localStorage.getItem('sm-analytics') === 'off';
      } catch {}
      checkbox.addEventListener('change', () => {
        try {
          localStorage.setItem('sm-analytics', checkbox.checked ? 'off' : 'on');
          if (checkbox.checked) sessionStorage.removeItem('sm-attribution');
        } catch {}
      });
    }
  </script>
</Layout>
